Manage the hard quota of buckets: writes that would exceed it are refused.
The quota is a setting of the Nexo Admin API (admin:SetBucketQuota).

Usage:
  nexoctl quota [flags]
  nexoctl quota [command]

Available Commands:
  clear       Remove the quota of a bucket
  info        Show the quota of a bucket
  set         Set the hard quota of a bucket

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for quota

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl quota [command] --help" for more information about a command.
